# Angular UI

- Feature code lives under `ui/src/app/<feature>/` with colocated `.ts` / `.html` / `.scss`.
- Use standalone components, SCSS for `styleUrl`, and lazy `loadComponent` routes (`app.routes.ts`).
- Prefer `inject()` and signals; mirror the nearest existing feature for structure and naming.
- Shared HTTP helpers and cross-feature services go in `ui/src/app/services/`; models in `models/` or feature-local interfaces.
- Do not add unit/e2e tests unless the user explicitly asks (workspace generators set runners to none).
- Keep API base URLs consistent with existing services (`http://localhost:3000/api/...`) until an environment abstraction exists.
- When extracting shared UI/API types, prefer `packages/*` over duplicating models across `ui` and `api`.
